<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bridgetown</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bridgetown is the capital and main port of Barbados, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlisle">Carlisle</a> Bay on the island's south-west coast. Founded by English settlers in 1628, it became a centre of the Atlantic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> and the seat of British governors in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. Its historic centre and garrison were made a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2011.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bridgetown.jpg" alt="Bridgetown" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: P.Lechien · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bridgetown_aerial.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
